        "date": "2026-11-21T17:47:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge a wire taper at the model's chord tolerance, refuse an undercut\n\nA constant-taper Wire Contour is now judged under the model's chord\ntolerance (the importer's promise, or a coarser recorded chord). The\ngenerator lays the wire from one height's section, so the facets at\nother heights stand off the true cone by up to that chord, and a cone\nwas refused at its true angle.\n\nA new undercut law judges the last pass of such a cut: a move that cuts\na drafted wall at one height and stands off it past the tolerance at\nanother blocks the post by name. A vertical wall cut at a taper is a\nstated relief and is not judged.\n\nFixes #3210\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
